.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_DEVI_CONFIG_VHCI 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_devi_config_vhci
.Nd create and attach a virtual host controller node
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "dev_info_t *"
.Fo ndi_devi_config_vhci
.Fa "char *drvname"
.Fa "int flags"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va drvname
Null-terminated name of the virtual HCI driver.
.It Va flags
Reserved; pass zero.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBndi_devi_config_vhci()\fP obtains the virtual host controller node for
\fBdrvname\fP.
If the driver's device list already has a node, that node is returned.
Otherwise the function allocates a persistent node under the root nexus,
marks it as a virtual HCI, initializes and attaches it, and links it into the
tree.
This is an internal multipathing enumeration helper used to avoid ordinary
cross-subtree enumeration during module initialization or attachment.
It is not a general-purpose child-node constructor.
.Pp
The framework retains the created node and driver.
The returned pointer does not carry a new reference for the caller to release.
The \fBflags\fP argument is unused; pass zero.
.Sh CONTEXT
These functions may be called from user or kernel context.
They may sleep.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The function returns the virtual HCI node, or \fBNULL\fP if the driver
name is unknown or initialization or attachment fails.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_devi_alloc 9F ,
.Xr ndi_hold_devi 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
